# NoID Privacy Workstation — .gitignore
#
# Rationale: keep repo lean + prevent accidental commits of secrets,
# build artifacts, host-specific data, and large binaries.
# GitHub.com warns above 50 MiB and blocks regular Git-repository files above
# 100 MiB. Release assets are a separate surface and must each be under 2 GiB.

# ============================================================
# Build artifacts + large binaries
# ============================================================

# Fedora base netinst ISO (about 1.2 GB): placed manually under /var/tmp or
# ~/Downloads and authenticated by scripts/verify-fedora-base-iso.sh; do NOT
# commit it.
image/*.iso
image/*.img
image/*.qcow2
image/*.raw
image/*.vmdk

# Build output (livemedia-creator working directory + final ISO)
*.log
build/
output/
build-output/
build-archive/
*.iso
*.img
*.iso.sha256
*.iso.asc
*.iso.sig
SHA256SUMS
SHA256SUMS.asc
BUILD-ATTESTATION.txt
vm-test-signoff.txt

# Kickstart temp files
*.ks.bak
*.ks.orig
*.ks.bak-*

# Per-file backups (snapshots before refactors)
*.bak-*
.bak-*

# ============================================================
# Secrets + credentials (MUST never leak)
# ============================================================

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# SSH keys
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
id_dsa
*.pem
*.key
authorized_keys
known_hosts

# GPG keys
*.gpg
*.asc
!docs/*.asc
secring.*
pubring.*
trustdb.gpg

# LUKS headers + recovery keys (CRITICAL — never commit)
luks-header-*.bin
luks-header-*.img
*-recovery.key
*-recovery.txt
luks-backup-*

# AWS/cloud credentials
.aws/
.gcp/
.azure/
credentials
credentials.json

# Passwords + tokens
*password*
*passwd*
*.token
.netrc

# ============================================================
# Host-specific data (private info — sanitize before commit)
# ============================================================

# Host audit dumps (raw captures — contain MACs, UUIDs, VPN keys,
# hostnames, installed-package histories, kernel versions of a specific
# reference host). They must never be committed or shipped.
discovery/reference/
discovery/*.txt
discovery/kspp-live-audit.json

# Per-module design rationale lives in each snippet's header/body. The
# patterns above are a defensive guard against raw host-audit dumps under
# discovery/.

# Backups of live /etc configs
etc-backup-*/
configs-snapshot-*/
backups/

# Local agent/editor session state. NOT part of the public repo.
CONTINUE.md
.claude/
.claude-*


# ============================================================
# Editor + OS artifacts
# ============================================================

# Editor swap + backup files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*

# macOS/Linux filesystem noise
.DS_Store
.Trash-*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Shell history / caches
.bash_history
.zsh_history
.sh_history

# ============================================================
# Test / CI artifacts
# ============================================================

tests/*.log
tests/output/
.shellcheck.cache

# ============================================================
# Re-include files matched by the broad patterns above:
# explicit negative patterns where those globs are too greedy
# ============================================================

# Keep these committed even though their patterns could match
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!docs/*.md
!kickstart/snippets/*.ks
!tests/*.sh
!tests/README.md

# branding/SHA256SUMS is the manifest
# of all branding asset hashes. Module 32 fetches it at build time
# and SHA-verifies each branding payload before installing into the
# image. The generic `SHA256SUMS` rule above (intended for build-output/
# and build-archive/ ISO checksums) would otherwise hide this.
!branding/SHA256SUMS

# Build logs never belong in kickstart/snippets/: scripts/build-iso.sh keeps
# livemedia/program/virt-install logs in its private stage directory and
# copies them to the failure directory. Snippet-dir copies are stale by
# definition and should be cleaned between builds.
kickstart/snippets/livemedia.log
kickstart/snippets/virt-install.log
kickstart/snippets/program.log
kickstart/snippets/*.log

# Test scratch trees. Tests create executable scratch directories outside the
# checkout (tests/lib.sh make_exec_tmpdir). This pattern is a backstop for a
# checkout-local `.test-*` tree left by an interrupted run: untracked is
# not enough, because a concurrent `git add -A` could commit it, so the
# pattern is ignored and tests/00-compose-sources.sh refuses both new in-tree
# scratch directories and tracked ones.
.test-*/
